 "methodology": "For each server in the official MCP Registry that lists at least one remote URL, we test the first remote URL only (identical URLs are checked once) with a single attempt per week: one MCP initialize JSON-RPC POST (protocol 2025-06-18; JSON and SSE responses accepted), 10 s timeout, 256 KB body cap. If it succeeds without authentication we send notifications/initialized and one tools/list to count tools (first page only); no tool is ever called. Legacy SSE-type remotes get a GET and are classed reachable if an event stream starts within 5 s (no tool count). Caveats: a single attempt means transient failures (timeouts, 5xx, rate limits) can be counted as broken; auth_required (HTTP 401/403 or a WWW-Authenticate header) means the endpoint is alive but needs credentials, so we cannot tell whether it works for authorised users; servers listing several remotes are judged by the first only; registry entries can be stale. Checked from a single network location."
}